# Normalise line endings in the repository.
#
# Without this, `core.autocrlf` on Windows checks source files out with CRLF, and
# several tests read source files as text and search them for exact strings — for
# example `windows/tests/rendererWiring.test.ts` looks for a declaration ending in
# "\n}\n", and `windows/tests/languageCatalog.test.ts` parses the macOS Swift
# catalogue with regular expressions. Those searches silently miss under CRLF: the
# renderer-wiring test threw "could not find the end of: function mountMain(" on
# windows-latest while passing on macOS, so it had never actually run on the platform
# it was written for.
#
# Forcing LF makes a checkout identical everywhere and removes the whole class of
# problem rather than one instance of it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be line-ending converted.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.jpg binary
*.woff2 binary
*.zip binary

# Keep generated and vendored trees out of language statistics and diffs.
package-lock.json -diff linguist-generated
